{"seq":12,"trial_id":"v03-installer-dev-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-30T15:22:55.948Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"a0e373da302e84152a37edd515de9ce4e4123501b8fdf27fb5164799dc5507dc","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","text":"Here are the QFL ticket numbers I found in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**: Moss's Sunday prep for Ruth (5 Oct 2025, `dev/agent-notes/2025-10-05-north-sunday`). Thea Ramaswell submitted it on 4 Oct 2025 about gatehouse kiosk SMS bay assignments at the Eau Claire yard. The same note lists it again as an action item for 6 Oct.\n2. **#4419**: Moss's North cheat sheet, undated (`dev/agent-notes/north-account-cheatsheet`). It covers gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14, and says it was escalated to tier-2 product support.\n\nTwo things to check before the weekly notes go out:\n- #4419 also appears in a note by Marcus Lindqvist, not Moss (14 Jul 2025, \"Q2 expansion wrap\"). That note describes it as Gate 3 printer lag, not the Door 14 scanner issue. I left that note out since it isn't Moss's, but the number and description may need reconciling.\n- The search runs keyword-only, so a note that describes a ticket without using \"QFL\" or \"Quarrendon\" could be missed.\n\nMoss's other QFL notes (9/14/2025 pipeline digest and 3/23/2026 renewal check-in) don't include ticket numbers. Moss's Central notes mention #4409 and #4412, but those are for a different dealer account, so I didn't include them."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03INS0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
